title: "Artificial General Machines: a falsification study of architectural self-determination"
message: "If you use this laboratory or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Mr-Infect"
    email: "mrinfectanalyst@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mr-Infect/artifical-general-machines"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
version: "0.3"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - architecture search
  - transfer learning
  - adaptive agents
  - negative result
  - pre-registered experiment
abstract: >
  A reproducible laboratory that tests whether a machine can learn transferable
  principles of computational organization (an "Artificial General Machine")
  against fixed, adaptive, search-based and memory-based agents. Three rounds of
  increasingly strict, pre-registered experiments (v0.1, v0.2, v0.3; 30 seeds)
  failed to separate the AGM from architecture search plus memory. The repository
  publishes the instrument, the raw analysis tables, the plots and the negative result.
